BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//ScriptureTools//BibleConverter//EN
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0533ad4d-7d00-4794-a9bc-4f07c15b9dae
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:1
DESCRIPTION:In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a5aad92d-121f-4681-9cd0-373c299f1ec5
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:2
DESCRIPTION:And the earth was without form, and void; and darkness was upon the face of the deep. And the Spirit of God moved upon the face of the waters.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b474c7ca-d54d-46b0-af13-ec0f05c45aaf
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:3
DESCRIPTION:And God said, Let there be light: and there was light.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:702d359d-f52d-41b1-b50b-ef485eeaf837
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:4
DESCRIPTION:And God saw the light, that it was good: and God divided the light from the darkness.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6a2bdf73-a135-4a9f-abe8-841de35ed3bc
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:5
DESCRIPTION:And God called the light Day, and the darkness he called Night. And the evening and the morning were the first day.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e98ac7ee-c54c-4ae8-8aef-b8bf7e70e69b
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:6
DESCRIPTION:And God said, Let there be a firmament in the midst of the waters, and let it divide the waters from the waters.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dd1521a1-4498-48a3-a320-1d4e4736bb72
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:7
DESCRIPTION:And God made the firmament, and divided the waters which were under the firmament from the waters which were above the firmament: and it was so.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:df1635e6-49fa-408d-9489-44f7e68ba610
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:8
DESCRIPTION:And God called the firmament Heaven. And the evening and the morning were the second day.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6f5f5ec6-ae24-429c-b78c-fc9e5ef505ad
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:9
DESCRIPTION:And God said, Let the waters under the heaven be gathered together unto one place, and let the dry land appear: and it was so.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:62a19d31-6b7c-4af8-9425-48efc038b4e7
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:10
DESCRIPTION:And God called the dry land Earth; and the gathering together of the waters called he Seas: and God saw that it was good.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fc8c63c1-dc24-4add-a70f-43d02ffc455e
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:11
DESCRIPTION:And God said, Let the earth bring forth grass, the herb yielding seed, and the fruit tree yielding fruit after his kind, whose seed is in itself, upon the earth: and it was so.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5372429a-017b-46a3-a609-20eb532c90f6
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:12
DESCRIPTION:And the earth brought forth grass, and herb yielding seed after his kind, and the tree yielding fruit, whose seed was in itself, after his kind: and God saw that it was good.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f52e8dfb-942c-41b2-ae0e-3b33a127e867
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:13
DESCRIPTION:And the evening and the morning were the third day.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a0330ce1-7fbe-4c93-8f6e-b0306c515955
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:14
DESCRIPTION:And God said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c696e7e9-6215-446f-9a6f-4ad341be7993
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:15
DESCRIPTION:And let them be for lights in the firmament of the heaven to give light upon the earth: and it was so.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5b22bc7c-023a-418f-8663-61acd84ae0b8
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:16
DESCRIPTION:And God made two great lights; the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night: he made the stars also.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ed97e322-4881-49be-832f-6ad66dcf0093
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:17
DESCRIPTION:And God set them in the firmament of the heaven to give light upon the earth,
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c13c2092-4e4e-4591-81cd-99f6fbb75a13
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:18
DESCRIPTION:And to rule over the day and over the night, and to divide the light from the darkness: and God saw that it was good.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7836bca5-91d6-4715-a0a6-95e24ec1eb03
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:19
DESCRIPTION:And the evening and the morning were the fourth day.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2f4aa19a-1ae2-4f94-b401-cc7710d5fdb1
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:20
DESCRIPTION:And God said, Let the waters bring forth abundantly the moving creature that hath life, and fowl that may fly above the earth in the open firmament of heaven.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3a4668ea-eb7c-4c12-a97d-1d74ab650b2f
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:21
DESCRIPTION:And God created great whales, and every living creature that moveth, which the waters brought forth abundantly, after their kind, and every winged fowl after his kind: and God saw that it was good.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f3d959e7-ecdd-432c-bc0b-19c70ed997c5
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:22
DESCRIPTION:And God blessed them, saying, Be fruitful, and multiply, and fill the waters in the seas, and let fowl multiply in the earth.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:599e4eb9-dd97-464a-b72b-0384c27bd4d9
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:23
DESCRIPTION:And the evening and the morning were the fifth day.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e06ddfeb-6516-4e29-b6ab-a74c5998f149
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:24
DESCRIPTION:And God said, Let the earth bring forth the living creature after his kind, cattle, and creeping thing, and beast of the earth after his kind: and it was so.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5affafa8-a9ff-46af-9409-935327227d42
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:25
DESCRIPTION:And God made the beast of the earth after his kind, and cattle after their kind, and every thing that creepeth upon the earth after his kind: and God saw that it was good.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:00d9a6d4-fe78-4340-ab8b-8ff3671a8425
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:26
DESCRIPTION:And God said, Let us make man in our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over the cattle, and over all the earth, and over every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3d44ff28-56a9-4a03-b158-1dd66ccd564e
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:27
DESCRIPTION:So God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ea7fcb8f-6dfd-4e71-8d2d-737e2691a769
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:28
DESCRIPTION:And God blessed them, and God said unto them, Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth, and subdue it: and have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over every living thing that moveth upon the earth.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2b2c5e89-c4aa-4da5-acab-3b9a8a3f269b
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:29
DESCRIPTION:And God said, Behold, I have given you every herb bearing seed, which is upon the face of all the earth, and every tree, in the which is the fruit of a tree yielding seed; to you it shall be for meat.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5fb95482-98b2-4279-843e-13dc6fafe085
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:30
DESCRIPTION:And to every beast of the earth, and to every fowl of the air, and to every thing that creepeth upon the earth, wherein there is life, I have given every green herb for meat: and it was so.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2ae6bf41-0e82-40d8-9c0e-2448b90c02c3
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 1:31
DESCRIPTION:And God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. And the evening and the morning were the sixth day.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:31de97ce-b466-4a69-bd50-dd789b84e7b8
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:1
DESCRIPTION:Thus the heavens and the earth were finished, and all the host of them.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:451dfdf1-ef95-41e1-bcda-308a326fdc51
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:2
DESCRIPTION:And on the seventh day God ended his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had made.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b3dc5a93-c507-4d2f-a0ee-4f40193f1719
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:3
DESCRIPTION:And God blessed the seventh day, and sanctified it: because that in it he had rested from all his work which God created and made.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c16e353d-4144-4d6d-af5f-7e4d3db4a94e
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:4
DESCRIPTION:These are the generations of the heavens and of the earth when they were created, in the day that the LORD God made the earth and the heavens,
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ff49dad4-e25e-4560-8e90-44f6be4b0e44
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:5
DESCRIPTION:And every plant of the field before it was in the earth, and every herb of the field before it grew: for the LORD God had not caused it to rain upon the earth, and there was not a man to till the ground.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ff1ca579-5bcc-4a9e-88e2-228fb971b963
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:6
DESCRIPTION:But there went up a mist from the earth, and watered the whole face of the ground.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5fc3ec4a-9d9b-4d29-8281-52c05f3d49e4
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:7
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:467da215-fb6f-4d15-940e-11b49b416e2d
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:8
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God planted a garden eastward in Eden; and there he put the man whom he had formed.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cf772f7c-33d8-49ee-a00f-36a49a122a9d
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:9
DESCRIPTION:And out of the ground made the LORD God to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:42c84a90-6cd7-4840-8354-5e19b701ec87
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:10
DESCRIPTION:And a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became into four heads.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7cc0ad6b-5fd2-4319-bdc7-2852eaae6db5
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:11
DESCRIPTION:The name of the first is Pison: that is it which compasseth the whole land of Havilah, where there is gold;
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5dd83a74-11f6-4b69-b4b0-e9ece652ddd9
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:12
DESCRIPTION:And the gold of that land is good: there is bdellium and the onyx stone.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d6aa3382-fe26-42ec-a5e8-99fcc08cd73e
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:13
DESCRIPTION:And the name of the second river is Gihon: the same is it that compasseth the whole land of Ethiopia.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d69ea8b2-4727-4b33-8706-74586f2c9bae
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:14
DESCRIPTION:And the name of the third river is Hiddekel: that is it which goeth toward the east of Assyria. And the fourth river is Euphrates.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:db13c13c-a65f-43b2-8808-df9d593b7f03
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:15
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God took the man, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f310bb31-59a8-4921-b06f-dcc34fdb674b
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:16
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God commanded the man, saying, Of every tree of the garden thou mayest freely eat:
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cb2788c1-ff71-4881-b512-cf12bd20f5a1
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:17
DESCRIPTION:But of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it: for in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f49c2e48-e4b8-4c8e-8c33-b463d0dabc5b
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:18
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God said, It is not good that the man should be alone; I will make him an help meet for him.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:514ab1d7-2116-461e-81b8-a6f2cf6ccda8
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:19
DESCRIPTION:And out of the ground the LORD God formed every beast of the field, and every fowl of the air; and brought them unto Adam to see what he would call them: and whatsoever Adam called every living creature, that was the name thereof.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:78a1b9f2-b1bb-4507-ba43-3b69555dbce4
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:20
DESCRIPTION:And Adam gave names to all cattle, and to the fowl of the air, and to every beast of the field; but for Adam there was not found an help meet for him.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f44a8a81-5d8b-4b88-82a8-cbca2f477697
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:21
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam, and he slept: and he took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh instead thereof;
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:77f8247e-f69f-4632-bef5-10df773ef914
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:22
DESCRIPTION:And the rib, which the LORD God had taken from man, made he a woman, and brought her unto the man.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:91e0bf21-55b4-4d54-b1be-b23d03baa574
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:23
DESCRIPTION:And Adam said, This is now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh: she shall be called Woman, because she was taken out of Man.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0d968e56-6ff7-454a-8a1b-2ac6f495b234
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:24
DESCRIPTION:Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave unto his wife: and they shall be one flesh.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fe470261-17a5-475f-ad05-e4379f817120
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 2:25
DESCRIPTION:And they were both naked, the man and his wife, and were not ashamed.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:29ac1996-83e4-46cd-9c03-e6f61204dac8
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:1
DESCRIPTION:Now the serpent was more subtil than any beast of the field which the LORD God had made. And he said unto the woman, Yea, hath God said, Ye shall not eat of every tree of the garden?
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:351b9699-ef87-4f07-bccd-80e3140640ce
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:2
DESCRIPTION:And the woman said unto the serpent, We may eat of the fruit of the trees of the garden:
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5772dea1-15ef-459f-883c-b32d011a6c6b
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:3
DESCRIPTION:But of the fruit of the tree which is in the midst of the garden, God hath said, Ye shall not eat of it, neither shall ye touch it, lest ye die.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ec391247-95ec-44c7-b3fc-5372d99ac074
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:4
DESCRIPTION:And the serpent said unto the woman, Ye shall not surely die:
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:14d48159-8d98-4b9d-a720-73ebdcdca978
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:5
DESCRIPTION:For God doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c2efd261-7e91-412a-bebe-e9c98ce7d1f2
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:6
DESCRIPTION:And when the woman saw that the tree was good for food, and that it was pleasant to the eyes, and a tree to be desired to make one wise, she took of the fruit thereof, and did eat, and gave also unto her husband with her; and he did eat.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:63a515b7-d1f2-4943-ac79-b4b01a19ad4f
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:7
DESCRIPTION:And the eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked; and they sewed fig leaves together, and made themselves aprons.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6fd7bcac-1518-4150-821f-a72354959411
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:8
DESCRIPTION:And they heard the voice of the LORD God walking in the garden in the cool of the day: and Adam and his wife hid themselves from the presence of the LORD God amongst the trees of the garden.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:31d564fb-e933-4849-b60e-3f144ef566c7
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:9
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God called unto Adam, and said unto him, Where art thou?
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:548e7af5-401a-47c3-9ffa-ba99e14e0e66
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:10
DESCRIPTION:And he said, I heard thy voice in the garden, and I was afraid, because I was naked; and I hid myself.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:94333e1a-8a4f-421f-8304-c2db9c7f3be2
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:11
DESCRIPTION:And he said, Who told thee that thou wast naked? Hast thou eaten of the tree, whereof I commanded thee that thou shouldest not eat?
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9325ae76-0e5e-4391-84a5-9988ce734d2c
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:12
DESCRIPTION:And the man said, The woman whom thou gavest to be with me, she gave me of the tree, and I did eat.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:837ba507-5f74-4883-88d3-29f179bbf10f
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:13
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God said unto the woman, What is this that thou hast done? And the woman said, The serpent beguiled me, and I did eat.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9c0f3e4d-43ba-4789-b8e1-6a2799a4a0f3
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:14
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God said unto the serpent, Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field; upon thy belly shalt thou go, and dust shalt thou eat all the days of thy life:
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d9bef78c-8d78-4c7a-aad5-fcd344d6b2ea
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:15
DESCRIPTION:And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7e0f112d-5ba9-4f55-b9a6-2869d0c07f36
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:16
DESCRIPTION:Unto the woman he said, I will greatly multiply thy sorrow and thy conception; in sorrow thou shalt bring forth children; and thy desire shall be to thy husband, and he shall rule over thee.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:480b35ad-6d6b-4c9c-8267-4d036efbb740
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:17
DESCRIPTION:And unto Adam he said, Because thou hast hearkened unto the voice of thy wife, and hast eaten of the tree, of which I commanded thee, saying, Thou shalt not eat of it: cursed is the ground for thy sake; in sorrow shalt thou eat of it all the days of thy life;
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a9dc589c-edc7-473b-bdbf-cbfda955e19d
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:18
DESCRIPTION:Thorns also and thistles shall it bring forth to thee; and thou shalt eat the herb of the field;
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c22dca99-1b0d-43ec-8b18-98afe088c8ce
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:19
DESCRIPTION:In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:745f8734-21d9-4c35-ad85-050a5de8def4
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:20
DESCRIPTION:And Adam called his wife’s name Eve; because she was the mother of all living.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:21e2b75b-0179-466e-9a36-3d186566f968
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:21
DESCRIPTION:Unto Adam also and to his wife did the LORD God make coats of skins, and clothed them.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:24bee9ca-4eae-4940-b55d-124ebfd98948
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:22
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD God said, Behold, the man is become as one of us, to know good and evil: and now, lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever:
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:10e2fb06-e83d-4681-a94f-9f08f7abc7d6
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:23
DESCRIPTION:Therefore the LORD God sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cc62bf9c-0561-48da-a580-eedefffc1541
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 3:24
DESCRIPTION:So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:da350268-124b-4ba3-93ec-542d8d2f8044
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:1
DESCRIPTION:And Adam knew Eve his wife; and she conceived, and bare Cain, and said, I have gotten a man from the LORD.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:98863ded-fa0f-4180-ac33-f8b460aaf64c
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:2
DESCRIPTION:And she again bare his brother Abel. And Abel was a keeper of sheep, but Cain was a tiller of the ground.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:166e607c-4cce-492b-a78c-65901b4d01da
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:3
DESCRIPTION:And in process of time it came to pass, that Cain brought of the fruit of the ground an offering unto the LORD.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:924fadc6-d5df-46a7-ab77-39b3a06ec7c7
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:4
DESCRIPTION:And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And the LORD had respect unto Abel and to his offering:
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1bc05307-fb38-4b09-878a-1b0a23cb98ea
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:5
DESCRIPTION:But unto Cain and to his offering he had not respect. And Cain was very wroth, and his countenance fell.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8d46de6f-4942-433a-90ed-4aa88c6458b5
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:6
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD said unto Cain, Why art thou wroth? and why is thy countenance fallen?
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:525ec22a-fc6c-4638-b6d6-359e50992121
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:7
DESCRIPTION:If thou doest well, shalt thou not be accepted? and if thou doest not well, sin lieth at the door. And unto thee shall be his desire, and thou shalt rule over him.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6d9bc774-5145-41e3-955a-1eb4b383e4d9
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:8
DESCRIPTION:And Cain talked with Abel his brother: and it came to pass, when they were in the field, that Cain rose up against Abel his brother, and slew him.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d5edfc43-fe25-40a5-87e8-bd87678d92d3
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:9
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD said unto Cain, Where is Abel thy brother? And he said, I know not: Am I my brother’s keeper?
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:68ab658e-9e33-454e-8cea-e12d1d4623cd
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:10
DESCRIPTION:And he said, What hast thou done? the voice of thy brother’s blood crieth unto me from the ground.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:07366323-15d6-44d1-9d62-53241be4d4fd
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:11
DESCRIPTION:And now art thou cursed from the earth, which hath opened her mouth to receive thy brother’s blood from thy hand;
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:abcd4342-8471-47eb-9fae-54d2c84c1a59
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:12
DESCRIPTION:When thou tillest the ground, it shall not henceforth yield unto thee her strength; a fugitive and a vagabond shalt thou be in the earth.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:13767d53-333b-41b8-9cf4-567cdebfc4a5
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:13
DESCRIPTION:And Cain said unto the LORD, My punishment is greater than I can bear.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1af21b9d-a65a-42db-b87e-79770e148cb8
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:14
DESCRIPTION:Behold, thou hast driven me out this day from the face of the earth; and from thy face shall I be hid; and I shall be a fugitive and a vagabond in the earth; and it shall come to pass, that every one that findeth me shall slay me.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a85e6d9a-a444-4593-b3cf-59a49f72a794
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:15
DESCRIPTION:And the LORD said unto him, Therefore whosoever slayeth Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold. And the LORD set a mark upon Cain, lest any finding him should kill him.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:566339cc-e23c-41a9-8e26-9556501bb349
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:16
DESCRIPTION:And Cain went out from the presence of the LORD, and dwelt in the land of Nod, on the east of Eden.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8d0c3820-e3e7-4a74-a3c2-252ff3b50101
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:17
DESCRIPTION:And Cain knew his wife; and she conceived, and bare Enoch: and he builded a city, and called the name of the city, after the name of his son, Enoch.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2701288a-4847-436d-a364-7819dc5dddb4
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:18
DESCRIPTION:And unto Enoch was born Irad: and Irad begat Mehujael: and Mehujael begat Methusael: and Methusael begat Lamech.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:311be653-f517-4756-a56d-37d7037f66eb
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:19
DESCRIPTION:And Lamech took unto him two wives: the name of the one was Adah, and the name of the other Zillah.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3322a9e2-3031-4197-b0ae-bd4248c49d35
DTSTAMP:20260504T000000Z
SUMMARY:GEN 4:20
DESCRIPTION:And Adah bare Jabal: he was the father of such as dwell in tents, and of such as have cattle.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
